      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 15 - Shareholders' Equity",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "During fiscal year 2023, we repurchased 63 million shares for $10.04 billion. Since the inception of our share repurchase program through January 29, 2023, we have repurchased an aggregate of 1.10 billion shares under our share repurchase program for a total cost of $17.12 billion.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA FY2023 Share Repurchase Activity",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 15 - Shareholders' Equity",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "As of January 29, 2023, we were authorized, subject to certain specifications, to repurchase an additional $7.23 billion of shares through December 2023.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Remaining Repurchase Authorization (Jan 2023)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 15 - Shareholders' Equity",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "During fiscal years 2023, 2022, and 2021, we paid $398 million, $399 million, and $395 million in cash dividends to our shareholders, respectively.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA FY2023 Cash Dividends",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 12 - Debt",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "In June 2021, March 2020, and September 2016, we issued a total of $5.00 billion, $5.00 billion, and $2.00 billion aggregate principal of senior notes, respectively. The net proceeds from these offerings were $4.98 billion, $4.97 billion, and $1.98 billion, respectively, after deducting debt discount and issuance costs.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA June 2021 $5.0B Senior Notes Issuance",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 13 - Commitments and Contingencies",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The plaintiffs in the putative securities class action lawsuit, captioned 4:18-cv-07669-HSG, initially filed on December 21, 2018 in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California, and titled In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation, filed an amended complaint on May 13, 2020. The amended complaint asserted that NVIDIA and certain NVIDIA executives violated Section 10(b) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, or the Exchange Act, and SEC Rule 10b-5, by making materially false or misleading statements related to channel inventory and the impact of cryptocurrency mining on GPU demand between May 10, 2017 and November 14, 2018.",
            "entity_name": "In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 13 - Commitments and Contingencies",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "On March 2, 2021, the district court granted NVIDIA's motion to dismiss the complaint without leave to amend, entered judgment in favor of NVIDIA and closed the case. On March 30, 2021, plaintiffs filed an appeal from judgment in the United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit, case number 21-15604. Oral argument on the appeal was held on May 10, 2022.",
            "entity_name": "In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 13 - Commitments and Contingencies",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative lawsuit pending in the United States District Court for the Northern District of California, captioned 4:19-cv-00341-HSG, initially filed January 18, 2019 and titled In re NVIDIA Corporation Consolidated Derivative Litigation, was stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action. On February 22, 2022, the court administratively closed the case, but stated that it would reopen the case once the appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action is resolved.",
            "entity_name": "In re NVIDIA Corporation Consolidated Derivative Litigation",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 13 - Commitments and Contingencies",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative actions initially filed September 24, 2019 and pending in the United States District Court for the District of Delaware, Lipchitz v. Huang, et al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01795-UNA) and Nelson v. Huang, et. al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01798- UNA), remain stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action.",
            "entity_name": "Lipchitz v. Huang et al.",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 13 - Commitments and Contingencies",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The putative derivative actions initially filed September 24, 2019 and pending in the United States District Court for the District of Delaware, Lipchitz v. Huang, et al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01795-UNA) and Nelson v. Huang, et. al. (Case No. 1:19-cv-01798- UNA), remain stayed pending resolution of the plaintiffs' appeal in the In Re NVIDIA Corporation Securities Litigation action.",
            "entity_name": "Nelson v. Huang et al.",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 17 - Segment Information",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "The Compute & Networking segment includes our Data Center accelerated computing platform; networking; automotive AI Cockpit, autonomous driving development agreements, and autonomous vehicle solutions; electric vehicle computing platforms; Jetson for robotics and other embedded platforms; and NVIDIA AI Enterprise and other software; and CMP.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Compute & Networking Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note_ref": "Note 17 - Segment Information",
              "section_type": "Item_15"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "The Graphics segment includes GeForce GPUs for gaming and PCs, the GeForce NOW game streaming service and related infrastructure, and solutions for gaming platforms; Quadro/NVIDIA RTX GPUs for enterprise workstation graphics; vGPU software for cloud-based visual and virtual computing; automotive platforms for infotainment systems; and Omniverse Enterprise software for building and operating metaverse and 3D internet applications.",
            "entity_name": "NVDA Graphics Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
